 - Optional - It is a container for object used to avoid Nullpointerexception
  Problem Code:
     String str = null;
     sop(str.length);
  The problem here is you will get Nullpointerexception.
  Syntax:
     Optional<String> oStr = Optional.ofNullable(str);
     if(oStr.isPresent()){
        oStr.get().length();
     }

     get(): for getting value from optional.
     isPresent(): This checks if the optional container is having data or not.
     ifPresent(lambda): exectes the lambda when there is value else it wont execute lambda.
     orElseThrow(exception): if value is present then get the value, else throw the exception mentioned.

